  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"880\" data-end=\"1234\">\n<li data-start=\"880\" data-end=\"1069\">\n<p data-start=\"882\" data-end=\"1069\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"882\" data-end=\"894\">Detected</strong>: Suggests presence of fungal DNA. Indicates <strong data-start=\"939\" data-end=\"976\">active or recent fungal infection</strong>; common fungi detected include <em data-start=\"1008\" data-end=\"1017\">Candida</em>, <em data-start=\"1019\" data-end=\"1032\">Aspergillus</em>, <em data-start=\"1034\" data-end=\"1048\">Cryptococcus</em>, <em data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1063\">Histoplasma</em>, etc.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1234\">\n<p data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1234\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1088\">Not Detected</strong>: No fungal DNA found in the sample. Does not completely rule out infection&mdash;consider clinical correlation and repeat testing if suspicion remains.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote data-start=\"1236\" data-end=\"1414\">\n<p data-start=\"1238\" data-end=\"1414\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">PCR is particularly useful in <strong data-start=\"1268\" data-end=\"1298\">immunocompromised patients</strong> where early diagnosis is crucial. Complementary tests (KOH, fungal culture, antigen assays) may also aid diagnosis.</span></p>\n</blockquote>",
